A number congruent to $-8$ modulo $10$ has units digit $2$:

[
-8 \equiv 2 \pmod{10}
]

Reduce the three fractions separately:

[
\frac{44}{11}=4
]

[
\frac{110}{44}=\frac{5}{2}=2.5
]

[
\frac{44}{1100}=\frac{1}{25}=0.04
]

Reducing modulo $4$ gives:

[
c\equiv 21\equiv 1 \pmod{4}
]

After the third day, these give:

[
7+3=10,\quad 7\cdot2=14
]

[
8+3=11,\quad 8\cdot2=16
]

[
10+3=13,\quad 10\cdot2=20
]

Repeating a three-digit block twice gives:

[
\overline{FLYFLY}=1001\overline{FLY}
]

and

[
\overline{BUGBUG}=1001\overline{BUG}
]

The equation becomes:

[
8\cdot1001\overline{FLY}=1001\overline{BUG}
]

Divide by $1001$:

[
8\overline{FLY}=\overline{BUG}
]

The least possible fraction is:

[
\frac{4}{15}
]

Therefore the probability is:

[
\frac{300}{495}=\frac{20}{33}
]
